  "forward": "+Z (face/chest); Y up; ~1.82 m tall, feet at y=0",
  "notes": "SWAT mesh with its 24 native clips (prefixed Swat_) plus 35 clips retargeted offline from Quaternius Universal Animation Library 1+2 (Standard, in-place/non-root-motion) onto the SWAT rig (re-run: node .harness/retarget_run.mjs <out.glb> with a Vite server on :5189; page .harness/retarget_swat.html, sources in .harness/model_src/). Rig quirk: legs are children of Body, not Hips; feet (FootL/FootR) and pole targets (PTL/PTR) are children of Root (baked IK) - animate via clips only, and to attach a weapon use WristR (right hand). No prone/crawl clip exists (Prone_GetUp is lying on the back then standing). Native Swat_ gun clips are one-handed pistol-style pointing; no two-handed rifle hold - aim the rifle with a WristR attachment + upper-body override. Materials are flat-colour (Swat, Swat_Black, Skin, Visor): recolour Swat/Swat_Black per squad (e.g. olive/tan camo).",
